WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.729 --> 00:00:17.258
Robin was holding an important meeting with his men.

2
00:00:17.278 --> 00:00:21.421
"The Sheriff of Nottingham thinks he can trick me," he said.

3
00:00:21.441 --> 00:00:24.063
"Well, I have a few tricks of my own."

4
00:00:24.923 --> 00:00:27.845
He told his men to disguise themselves as peasants.

5
00:00:29.066 --> 00:00:31.608
"We're going to the sheriff's archery contest.

6
00:00:32.252 --> 00:00:33.933
And I'll win the gold arrow!"

7
00:00:33.953 --> 00:00:36.414
"Hooray for Robin!"

8
00:00:37.074 --> 00:00:37.814
shouted the men.

9
00:00:39.075 --> 00:00:41.176
The day came for the archery contest.

10
00:00:42.076 --> 00:00:44.177
Many people gathered on the town green.

11
00:00:44.997 --> 00:00:48.659
Knights, ladies, and wealthy merchants sat on one side.

12
00:00:49.399 --> 00:00:51.420
Peasants and beggars stood on the other.

13
00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.881
A raised platform was placed near the targets.

14
00:00:55.702 --> 00:00:57.742
That was for the sheriff and his party.

15
00:00:58.783 --> 00:01:01.324
The sheriff rode toward the green on his white horse.

16
00:01:02.208 --> 00:01:07.272
He was dressed in fine clothing—a purple velvet cap and purple velvet robes.

17
00:01:08.573 --> 00:01:10.554
A gold chain hung from his neck.

18
00:01:11.875 --> 00:01:17.038
A beautiful woman dressed in blue velvet robes trimmed with feathers rode beside him.

19
00:01:18.339 --> 00:01:21.361
The sheriff sat down and peered eagerly at the crowd.

20
00:01:22.482 --> 00:01:25.364
"Robin Hood must be here somewhere," he said.

21
00:01:25.384 --> 00:01:27.005
"I've never met him.

22
00:01:27.606 --> 00:01:30.648
But I know he and his men always wear green."

23
00:01:31.464 --> 00:01:34.305
A large group of archers was ready to compete.

24
00:01:34.906 --> 00:01:39.288
The crowd began cheering for their favorites, and then a man blew a horn.

25
00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.409
The contest began!

26
00:01:42.549 --> 00:01:45.991
After several rounds of shooting only five men were left.

27
00:01:50.133 --> 00:01:51.793
Three were famous archers.

28
00:01:52.574 --> 00:01:53.534
Everyone knew them.

29
00:01:54.295 --> 00:01:56.856
A fourth man was a stranger dressed in blue.

30
00:01:57.804 --> 00:02:02.026
The fifth man was another stranger who wore ragged red clothes.

31
00:02:02.046 --> 00:02:05.447
"Hmm," said the sheriff.

32
00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:08.588
"One of those strangers must be Robin Hood.

33
00:02:09.189 --> 00:02:09.869
Do you see him?"

34
00:02:10.149 --> 00:02:13.571
he asked one of his men, who knew the outlaw and could recognize him.

35
00:02:13.591 --> 00:02:18.693
"No, Robin is not here," replied the man.

36
00:02:18.713 --> 00:02:22.354
"Robin is taller than that man in blue.

37
00:02:23.014 --> 00:02:26.696
The man in red has brown hair and an eye patch.

38
00:02:27.716 --> 00:02:31.700
Robin's hair is blond and his eyesight is quite sharp."

39
00:02:33.461 --> 00:02:35.583
The sheriff hit his leg in anger.

40
00:02:35.603 --> 00:02:38.245
"So Robin Hood didn't dare to show up!"

41
00:02:38.545 --> 00:02:39.026
he said.

42
00:02:39.046 --> 00:02:42.709
"Well, then he's a coward as well as a thief!"

43
00:02:43.649 --> 00:02:45.991
Soon only two archers remained.

44
00:02:46.812 --> 00:02:51.296
They were the famous archer, Adam of Dell, and the stranger in red.

45
00:02:52.336 --> 00:02:54.258
Each man had one last shot.

46
00:02:54.919 --> 00:02:59.053
First, Adam took aim and struck the target close to the center.

47
00:02:59.754 --> 00:03:00.895
The crowd cheered.

48
00:03:03.796 --> 00:03:05.657
Next it was the stranger's turn.

49
00:03:06.198 --> 00:03:09.059
He picked up his bow and slowly took aim.

50
00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:13.502
The arrow zipped through the air and struck the target's center.

51
00:03:15.143 --> 00:03:17.964
Everyone stood up and clapped for the ragged archer.

52
00:03:18.705 --> 00:03:21.707
Adam of Dell took a long breath and shook his head.

53
00:03:21.727 --> 00:03:24.008
"I'm finished shooting for the day.

54
00:03:24.748 --> 00:03:27.230
For no one can match this stranger's shot."

55
00:03:27.710 --> 00:03:29.972
With that, he put down his bow.

56
00:03:31.433 --> 00:03:33.634
The sheriff stepped down from the platform.

57
00:03:34.375 --> 00:03:37.457
He presented the gold arrow to the stranger in red.

58
00:03:37.477 --> 00:03:39.839
"Here, good fellow, take your prize.

59
00:03:40.359 --> 00:03:41.040
What's your name?"

60
00:03:41.060 --> 00:03:46.543
"Um, they call me Jock of Teviotdale," said the archer.

61
00:03:46.563 --> 00:03:51.387
"You're the best archer I've ever seen," said the sheriff.

62
00:03:51.407 --> 00:03:54.998
"In fact, I'd like you to join my household.

63
00:03:55.718 --> 00:03:59.001
If you work for me, I'll provide you with clothes, food, and lodging.

64
00:03:59.582 --> 00:04:00.563
What do you say to that?"

65
00:04:01.384 --> 00:04:03.365
The stranger laughed loudly.

66
00:04:03.385 --> 00:04:06.828
"No man will ever be my master!"

67
00:04:07.309 --> 00:04:07.789
he said.

68
00:04:07.809 --> 00:04:11.573
"I like to do what I want to do."

69
00:04:12.413 --> 00:04:14.375
The sheriff was very insulted.

70
00:04:14.395 --> 00:04:17.478
"What a rude response.

71
00:04:18.359 --> 00:04:19.420
Now get out of here!"

72
00:04:21.436 --> 00:04:25.700
Later that day a group of ragged men gathered in Sherwood Forest.

73
00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:30.964
They congratulated Robin for his fine performance at the archery contest.

74
00:04:31.664 --> 00:04:35.107
"It'll take a while to get this brown dye out of my hair."

75
00:04:35.748 --> 00:04:38.150
Robin laughed as he removed his eye patch.

76
00:04:40.191 --> 00:04:44.375
While his men sat down to eat, Robin took Little John aside.

77
00:04:44.395 --> 00:04:50.560
"The sheriff thinks Robin Hood is a coward because I didn't show up today," said Robin.

78
00:04:51.488 --> 00:04:54.409
"I wish he knew who really won his gold arrow."

79
00:04:54.429 --> 00:04:57.210
"Don't worry," said Little John.

80
00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.211
"I'll take care of that."

81
00:05:02.172 --> 00:05:05.314
The next day the sheriff was hosting a meal at his house.

82
00:05:06.074 --> 00:05:10.716
"I was surprised Robin Hood didn't show up at the contest yesterday," he said to his guests.

83
00:05:11.496 --> 00:05:13.817
Suddenly an arrow flew through the window.

84
00:05:13.837 --> 00:05:17.039
It fell onto the table, rattling the dishes.

85
00:05:17.059 --> 00:05:20.380
"Look, there's a note attached!"

86
00:05:20.796 --> 00:05:22.197
said one of the sheriff's men.

87
00:05:22.778 --> 00:05:24.359
He handed the note to the sheriff.

88
00:05:24.979 --> 00:05:26.721
The sheriff read it aloud.

89
00:05:27.241 --> 00:05:29.443
Who's the best archer in Nottingham?

90
00:05:30.163 --> 00:05:31.865
Who won your gold arrow?

91
00:05:32.645 --> 00:05:34.406
Why, Robin Hood, of course!

92
00:05:34.947 --> 00:05:39.410
The sheriff's face was red with anger as he threw the note on the ground.

93
00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:46.095
"I'll put Robin Hood in jail if it's the last thing I do!"
